{"id":"refine_20260929114620484","summary":"Saved the validated ARC marker-gap transformation as a global memory.","rationale":"The transformation was supported by multiple demonstrations with different grid sizes and palettes, and the predicted output for the test grid was confirmed correct.","expectedOutcome":"Future sessions can recognize this pattern and submit without spending attempts on unnecessary demo requests; validate by checking that only background cells strictly between aligned markers are filled.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_fill_gaps_between_aligned_markers","title":"ARC: fill gaps between aligned markers","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse markers of one color, preserve all input cells and fill with color 3 each background cell strictly between two markers in the same row or column. Equivalently, in every row and column, fill the gaps between consecutive markers, without extending beyond the outermost markers. This rule was validated on demonstrations with varied palettes and dimensions, and on a 17x3 test with markers at rows 1, 2, and 5 in the middle column: only rows 3 and 4 in that column were filled. When a task clearly matches this pattern, submit directly rather than requesting more demonstrations.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"This is a reusable task rule confirmed by multiple demonstrations and a correct test submission.","after":{"id":"arc_fill_gaps_between_aligned_markers","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: fill gaps between aligned markers","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse markers of one color, preserve all input cells and fill with color 3 each background cell strictly between two markers in the same row or column. Equivalently, in every row and column, fill the gaps between consecutive markers, without extending beyond the outermost markers. This rule was validated on demonstrations with varied palettes and dimensions, and on a 17x3 test with markers at rows 1, 2, and 5 in the middle column: only rows 3 and 4 in that column were filled. When a task clearly matches this pattern, submit directly rather than requesting more demonstrations.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:46:25.857Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:46:25.857Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115009322","summary":"Updated the global ARC memory to capture the validated marker-gap rule without assuming fixed background or marker colors.","rationale":"The existing memory records fixed background and marker colors, but the solved instance and its demo show those colors vary: background/marker were 8/5 in the demo and 0/6 in the test, while fill color 3 remained constant. The row-and-column gap-filling rule is validated by both.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can apply the reusable rule across palette variations: independently fill background cells strictly between aligned markers in each row and column with color 3, preserving markers and all other cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_fill_gaps_between_aligned_markers","title":"ARC: fill gaps between aligned markers (task-baf873fe)","content":"Validated Continual-ARC rule for task-baf873fe: In each row independently and each column independently, find lines containing at least two marker cells. Fill every background cell strictly between the outermost marker positions on that line with color 3; leave marker cells unchanged and do not alter cells outside those intervals. Do not assume fixed background or marker colors: observed pairs include background/marker 8/5 in the demo, 0/6 in the solved test, and 7/2 in an earlier instance. Fill color 3 was consistent. The rule was validated against the demo pair and the correctly submitted test.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Correct the prior memory's overly specific palette assumptions while preserving the validated transformation.","before":{"id":"arc_fill_gaps_between_aligned_markers","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: fill gaps between aligned markers","content":"Continual-ARC validated rule (task-baf873fe): Treat color 7 as background, color 2 as markers, and color 3 as the fill. On each row independently and each column independently, if there are at least two color-2 markers, fill every cell strictly between the first and last marker (the minimum and maximum marker coordinates) with color 3. Keep all marker cells color 2 and all cells outside these row/column spans unchanged. Take the union of horizontal and vertical fills; at crossings, color 3. Verified on a fresh 10x19 test grid with irregular markers and overlapping row/column spans; submitted correctly with zero wrong attempts. No demo was needed.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:46:25.857Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:49:13.686844+00:00","version":6},"after":{"id":"arc_fill_gaps_between_aligned_markers","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: fill gaps between aligned markers (task-baf873fe)","content":"Validated Continual-ARC rule for task-baf873fe: In each row independently and each column independently, find lines containing at least two marker cells. Fill every background cell strictly between the outermost marker positions on that line with color 3; leave marker cells unchanged and do not alter cells outside those intervals. Do not assume fixed background or marker colors: observed pairs include background/marker 8/5 in the demo, 0/6 in the solved test, and 7/2 in an earlier instance. Fill color 3 was consistent. The rule was validated against the demo pair and the correctly submitted test.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:46:25.857Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:14.822Z","version":7},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115034687","summary":"Updated the global task-baf873fe memory with the successful fresh-input validation and precise color-specific rule.","rationale":"A new 10×20 instance was solved correctly without demos or wrong attempts by filling only background cells strictly between the outermost markers on qualifying rows and columns.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can apply the validated transformation directly; validate by preserving markers and all cells outside those spans while changing only intervening background cells to color 3.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_fill_gaps_between_aligned_markers","title":"ARC: fill gaps between aligned markers (task-baf873fe)","content":"Validated Continual-ARC rule for task-baf873fe across distinct inputs, including a fresh 10×20 test solved correctly without demos or wrong attempts. Identify marker color 1 and background color 9. Independently for each row and each column containing at least two markers, fill only background cells strictly between the minimum and maximum marker positions with color 3. Preserve markers and all cells outside those spans unchanged. When this pattern is clear, demos are unnecessary.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Records an independently successful fresh-input application and the exact transformation and color constraints for future recurring instances.","before":{"id":"arc_fill_gaps_between_aligned_markers","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: fill gaps between aligned markers (task-baf873fe)","content":"Validated Continual-ARC rule for task-baf873fe: In each row independently and each column independently, find lines containing at least two marker cells. Fill every background cell strictly between the outermost marker positions on that line with color 3; leave marker cells unchanged and do not alter cells outside those intervals. Do not assume fixed background or marker colors: observed pairs include background/marker 8/5 in the demo, 0/6 in the solved test, and 7/2 in an earlier instance. Fill color 3 was consistent. The rule was validated against the demo pair and the correctly submitted test.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:46:25.857Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:14.822Z","version":7},"after":{"id":"arc_fill_gaps_between_aligned_markers","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: fill gaps between aligned markers (task-baf873fe)","content":"Validated Continual-ARC rule for task-baf873fe across distinct inputs, including a fresh 10×20 test solved correctly without demos or wrong attempts. Identify marker color 1 and background color 9. Independently for each row and each column containing at least two markers, fill only background cells strictly between the minimum and maximum marker positions with color 3. Preserve markers and all cells outside those spans unchanged. When this pattern is clear, demos are unnecessary.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:46:25.857Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:39.234Z","version":8},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120150970","summary":"Saved the validated Continual-ARC rule for task-a48c79e4 as a global memory.","rationale":"Two demos show color 1 marking a discrepant region in a repeated pattern, and the fresh test confirmed that changing only the anomalous cell to 1 was correct. The evidence supports preserving the other cells and avoiding a more specific unsupported rule.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of task-a48c79e4 can compare repeated structures, identify the mismatching patch, and apply the demonstrated color-1 marking; validate by changing only the indicated discrepancy and preserving all other cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark the discrepant patch in repeated patterns","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, two demonstrations show color 1 marking a discrepant region in a repeated/paired pattern: demo 1 adds color 1 at rows 3–4, columns 8–9; demo 2 adds color 1 at rows 3–6, columns 17–21 (zero-based indices). On the fresh 9×14 test, rows 0 and 4 were nearly identical solid 8-bars, except row 0, column 13 was 5 instead of 8. Changing only that cell to 1 and preserving every other cell was confirmed correct with zero wrong attempts. Reusable heuristic: compare repeated or paired structures, mark the anomalous/mismatching patch with 1, and preserve all other cells. Treat this as a heuristic supported by these examples, not a more specific universal rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global","domain":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-a48c79e4","validation":"confirmed correct on fresh test"},"reason":"Persists a reusable, task-qualified rule supported by two demonstrations and a correct fresh-test submission, without overstating the inferred transformation.","after":{"id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark the discrepant patch in repeated patterns","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, two demonstrations show color 1 marking a discrepant region in a repeated/paired pattern: demo 1 adds color 1 at rows 3–4, columns 8–9; demo 2 adds color 1 at rows 3–6, columns 17–21 (zero-based indices). On the fresh 9×14 test, rows 0 and 4 were nearly identical solid 8-bars, except row 0, column 13 was 5 instead of 8. Changing only that cell to 1 and preserving every other cell was confirmed correct with zero wrong attempts. Reusable heuristic: compare repeated or paired structures, mark the anomalous/mismatching patch with 1, and preserve all other cells. Treat this as a heuristic supported by these examples, not a more specific universal rule.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","domain":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-a48c79e4","validation":"confirmed correct on fresh test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120320671","summary":"Updated the global task-a48c79e4 memory with the successful test validation and clarified that color 1 marks blank trailing regions, not excess foreground.","rationale":"The previous memory described marking discrepant patches but did not make the operational rule clear. The demo and successful test establish that the blank suffix after a shortened aligned stripe is marked through the grid edge, while existing foreground remains unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can identify the shorter aligned stripe, mark only its corresponding blank trailing region with color 1 through the edge, and validate that all other cells are preserved.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, compare the aligned repeated stripe patterns and identify where one stripe ends earlier. Mark the blank trailing region after the shortened stripe with color 1, extending to the grid edge; preserve the existing foreground and all unrelated cells. Do not recolor foreground that extends farther in another aligned pattern. Validated on a 22×16 test: the top and bottom 2-row patterns matched through column 10; the top rows 0–1 had color 5 through columns 11–15, while the bottom rows 17–18 were blank there. The correct output changed only rows 17–18, columns 11–15, from 0 to 1. A demo likewise marked the background suffix after aligned stripes, leaving stripe foreground unchanged.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Clarifies the demonstrated transformation and records a successful test validation, correcting ambiguity in the earlier discrepant-patch description.","before":{"id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark the discrepant patch in repeated patterns","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, two demonstrations show color 1 marking a discrepant region in a repeated/paired pattern: demo 1 adds color 1 at rows 3–4, columns 8–9; demo 2 adds color 1 at rows 3–6, columns 17–21 (zero-based indices). On the fresh 9×14 test, rows 0 and 4 were nearly identical solid 8-bars, except row 0, column 13 was 5 instead of 8. Changing only that cell to 1 and preserving every other cell was confirmed correct with zero wrong attempts. Reusable heuristic: compare repeated or paired structures, mark the anomalous/mismatching patch with 1, and preserve all other cells. Treat this as a heuristic supported by these examples, not a more specific universal rule.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","domain":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-a48c79e4","validation":"confirmed correct on fresh test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, compare the aligned repeated stripe patterns and identify where one stripe ends earlier. Mark the blank trailing region after the shortened stripe with color 1, extending to the grid edge; preserve the existing foreground and all unrelated cells. Do not recolor foreground that extends farther in another aligned pattern. Validated on a 22×16 test: the top and bottom 2-row patterns matched through column 10; the top rows 0–1 had color 5 through columns 11–15, while the bottom rows 17–18 were blank there. The correct output changed only rows 17–18, columns 11–15, from 0 to 1. A demo likewise marked the background suffix after aligned stripes, leaving stripe foreground unchanged.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:03:28.304Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120444747","summary":"Updated the global task-a48c79e4 memory with the directly validated trailing-suffix rule.","rationale":"A demo and fresh test confirmed that color 1 replaces only background cells to the right of each stripe row’s rightmost foreground cell; internal gaps and unrelated rows remain unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can apply the validated transformation while preserving all cells except trailing background suffixes after stripe ends; validate by checking the changed cells and retaining full-width rows unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, identify horizontal stripe rows and their rightmost foreground cell. Recolor only trailing background cells to the right of that cell through the grid’s right edge with color 1. Preserve all existing foreground cells, internal gaps, and unrelated rows; a full-width stripe has no trailing suffix to change. Direct evidence: the demo changed the suffix after a 4-cell stripe and a 7-cell stripe to color 1 while leaving a full-width stripe unchanged. In a fresh test, two stripe rows with internal gaps ended at column 6; only columns 7–9 changed from background 8 to 1. The submission was correct with zero wrong attempts. Validate by ensuring no cells except blank trailing suffixes were changed.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Persist the successful demo and fresh-test evidence, clarifying the exact cells to recolor and the preservation constraints.","before":{"id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, compare the aligned repeated stripe patterns and identify where one stripe ends earlier. Mark the blank trailing region after the shortened stripe with color 1, extending to the grid edge; preserve the existing foreground and all unrelated cells. Do not recolor foreground that extends farther in another aligned pattern. Validated on a 22×16 test: the top and bottom 2-row patterns matched through column 10; the top rows 0–1 had color 5 through columns 11–15, while the bottom rows 17–18 were blank there. The correct output changed only rows 17–18, columns 11–15, from 0 to 1. A demo likewise marked the background suffix after aligned stripes, leaving stripe foreground unchanged.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:03:28.304Z","version":2},"after":{"id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, identify horizontal stripe rows and their rightmost foreground cell. Recolor only trailing background cells to the right of that cell through the grid’s right edge with color 1. Preserve all existing foreground cells, internal gaps, and unrelated rows; a full-width stripe has no trailing suffix to change. Direct evidence: the demo changed the suffix after a 4-cell stripe and a 7-cell stripe to color 1 while leaving a full-width stripe unchanged. In a fresh test, two stripe rows with internal gaps ended at column 6; only columns 7–9 changed from background 8 to 1. The submission was correct with zero wrong attempts. Validate by ensuring no cells except blank trailing suffixes were changed.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:04:49.625Z","version":3},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120520892","summary":"Updated the global task-a48c79e4 memory with a fresh successful validation of the trailing-suffix marking rule.","rationale":"The trajectory confirms the existing rule on a new 24×15 input: among repeated aligned stripe motifs, only the shorter corresponding stripe row's background suffix was recolored, while the matched row pair and all other cells were preserved.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can recognize this repeated-stripe pattern and mark only the shorter aligned stripe's trailing background cells with color 1; validate by preserving all other cells, including suffixes on matched stripe rows.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, identify repeated horizontal stripe motifs and compare corresponding aligned stripe rows. When one corresponding stripe is shorter, recolor only its trailing background cells to the right of its rightmost foreground cell through the grid's right edge with color 1. Preserve all existing foreground and every other cell; do not mark ordinary background suffixes on matching stripe rows. Fresh validation: on a 24×15 input, repeated motifs appeared at rows 2–3 and 13–14 (0-indexed). Rows 2 and 13 matched exactly; row 3 extended through the right edge, while row 14 matched its prefix through column 10 and had background color 2 in columns 11–14. The correct output changed only row 14, columns 11–14, to color 1 and was solved with zero wrong attempts.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds an independent successful fresh-input validation and clarifies that only the shorter corresponding stripe's suffix is marked.","before":{"id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, identify horizontal stripe rows and their rightmost foreground cell. Recolor only trailing background cells to the right of that cell through the grid’s right edge with color 1. Preserve all existing foreground cells, internal gaps, and unrelated rows; a full-width stripe has no trailing suffix to change. Direct evidence: the demo changed the suffix after a 4-cell stripe and a 7-cell stripe to color 1 while leaving a full-width stripe unchanged. In a fresh test, two stripe rows with internal gaps ended at column 6; only columns 7–9 changed from background 8 to 1. The submission was correct with zero wrong attempts. Validate by ensuring no cells except blank trailing suffixes were changed.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:04:49.625Z","version":3},"after":{"id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, identify repeated horizontal stripe motifs and compare corresponding aligned stripe rows. When one corresponding stripe is shorter, recolor only its trailing background cells to the right of its rightmost foreground cell through the grid's right edge with color 1. Preserve all existing foreground and every other cell; do not mark ordinary background suffixes on matching stripe rows. Fresh validation: on a 24×15 input, repeated motifs appeared at rows 2–3 and 13–14 (0-indexed). Rows 2 and 13 matched exactly; row 3 extended through the right edge, while row 14 matched its prefix through column 10 and had background color 2 in columns 11–14. The correct output changed only row 14, columns 11–14, to color 1 and was solved with zero wrong attempts.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:05:26.520Z","version":4},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120555333","summary":"Updated the global task-a48c79e4 memory with a second successful validation of marking suffixes on shorter aligned stripes.","rationale":"The trajectory confirms the existing rule on a fresh 29×9 input with three left-aligned color-4 stripes of lengths 9, 5, and 4; only the background suffixes of the two shorter stripes were changed to color 1.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can apply the rule to each shorter aligned stripe independently and validate that the longest stripe and all unrelated cells remain unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, identify repeated aligned horizontal stripe motifs and compare their lengths. When aligned stripes have different lengths, recolor only the background suffix to the right of each shorter stripe's rightmost foreground cell through the grid's right edge with color 1. Preserve the longest stripe, all existing foreground, and every unrelated cell; do not mark suffixes on matching/full-length stripes. Validations: (1) On a 24×15 input, repeated motifs appeared at rows 2–3 and 13–14 (0-indexed). Rows 2 and 13 matched exactly; row 3 extended through the right edge, while row 14 matched its prefix through column 10 and had background color 2 in columns 11–14. The correct output changed only row 14, columns 11–14, to color 1. (2) On a 29×9 input, left-anchored color-4 stripes at rows 2, 15, and 23 had lengths 9, 5, and 4. The correct output changed only row 15, columns 5–8, and row 23, columns 4–8, to color 1. Both instances were solved with zero wrong attempts.","path":"general","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds a fresh, directly validated instance and clarifies applying the suffix-marking rule to each shorter aligned stripe.","before":{"id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, identify repeated horizontal stripe motifs and compare corresponding aligned stripe rows. When one corresponding stripe is shorter, recolor only its trailing background cells to the right of its rightmost foreground cell through the grid's right edge with color 1. Preserve all existing foreground and every other cell; do not mark ordinary background suffixes on matching stripe rows. Fresh validation: on a 24×15 input, repeated motifs appeared at rows 2–3 and 13–14 (0-indexed). Rows 2 and 13 matched exactly; row 3 extended through the right edge, while row 14 matched its prefix through column 10 and had background color 2 in columns 11–14. The correct output changed only row 14, columns 11–14, to color 1 and was solved with zero wrong attempts.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:05:26.520Z","version":4},"after":{"id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark blank trailing regions after aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, identify repeated aligned horizontal stripe motifs and compare their lengths. When aligned stripes have different lengths, recolor only the background suffix to the right of each shorter stripe's rightmost foreground cell through the grid's right edge with color 1. Preserve the longest stripe, all existing foreground, and every unrelated cell; do not mark suffixes on matching/full-length stripes. Validations: (1) On a 24×15 input, repeated motifs appeared at rows 2–3 and 13–14 (0-indexed). Rows 2 and 13 matched exactly; row 3 extended through the right edge, while row 14 matched its prefix through column 10 and had background color 2 in columns 11–14. The correct output changed only row 14, columns 11–14, to color 1. (2) On a 29×9 input, left-anchored color-4 stripes at rows 2, 15, and 23 had lengths 9, 5, and 4. The correct output changed only row 15, columns 5–8, and row 23, columns 4–8, to color 1. Both instances were solved with zero wrong attempts.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:55.692Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:06:00.366Z","version":5},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929121238689","summary":"Updated the global task-a48c79e4 memory with validated stripe-suffix behavior and a caution against blanket marking.","rationale":"The demos and correctly solved fresh instance support marking only trailing background cells after a genuinely shorter corresponding stripe; the first submission was wrong because it marked all four rows in the lower band.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should compare corresponding stripe lengths before changing cells, preserve matched stripes and unrelated cells, and validate that only shorter-stripe suffixes are recolored.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"task_a48c79e4_repeated_pattern_anomaly_marking","title":"Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4: mark trailing suffixes after shorter aligned stripes","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a48c79e4, identify repeated/aligned horizontal stripe motifs and compare the lengths of corresponding stripes. Recolor with color 1 only the trailing background suffix after a genuinely shorter stripe, toward the row's right edge through the unmatched tail. Preserve all unrelated cells and matched or equal-length stripes. Do not simply color the rightmost blank of every row, mark every row in a band that looks shorter, or infer the answer from endpoints alone. Validated demos: (1) In a 15x9 example, row 0's short color-0 stripe led to recoloring its trailing background c3–8; (2) in a 25x15 example, only trailing backgrounds in rows 1 (c10–14) and 8 (c13–14) were marked; (3) in a 16x11 example, row 0 c9–10 was marked after comparing its final aligned color-2 stripe with row 9. Fresh 28x22 validation: compare corresponding rightmost stripe runs in motif bands rows 6–9 and 21–24. Only rows 21 and 23 had shorter corresponding stripes, so change (21,21) and (23,21) from background 9 to 1 (zero-based row,column); rows 22 and 24 were equal-length and remain unchanged. The initial attempt that marked c21 in all four lower rows was incorrect. Always