{"id":"refine_20260929122347605","summary":"Updated the global task-3e903c7b memory with a fresh first-attempt validation and an explicit literal-color comparison rule.","rationale":"The submitted 12×15 instance was confirmed correct. It validates removing the uniform divider, comparing aligned cells by exact numeric color rather than foreground/background role, and using the left panel's background color for unequal pairs.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should produce a panel-sized grid with 3 only at literal cell matches and the left panel's background color elsewhere; validate divider removal, coordinate alignment, output dimensions, and palette handling.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"task_3e903c7b_panel_cell_match","title":"Continual-ARC task-3e903c7b: panel cell comparison","content":"For Continual-ARC task-3e903c7b, find the single uniform divider row or column, remove it, and split the remaining grid into two equal, aligned panels. Compare cells literally at the same row/column coordinates by numeric color: output 3 where the two values are exactly equal, and otherwise output the left panel's background color. Do not treat differently colored panel backgrounds as equal merely because both are backgrounds. Return only the panel dimensions. Fresh first-attempt validation: input 12×15 with divider column 7 (color 8) yielded a 12×7 output; the left panel background was 1, and the only equal-cell outputs (3) were at zero-based coordinates (0,3), (5,5), (10,2), and (10,4); every other output cell was 1. Preserve coordinate alignment when comparing across the divider.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds a successful fresh validation and clarifies the exact equality rule, preventing confusion between literal color equality and matching foreground/background roles.","before":{"id":"task_3e903c7b_panel_cell_match","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-3e903c7b: panel cell comparison","content":"For task-3e903c7b, find t