r output cell was 1. Preserve coordinate alignment when comparing across the divider.","path":"arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:14:27.773105+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:23:52.770Z","version":8},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929122647602","summary":"Created a global Continual-ARC memory for task-0c1f1b2f’s periodic stripe extrapolation rule.","rationale":"The five demonstrations show periodic patterns expanded across the grid from stripe clues, and the test submission verified that parallel diagonal markers can encode a checkerboard when their colors imply a period of two. The memory preserves the coordinate-phase and validation cautions while avoiding assumptions based only on palette or spacing.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can infer a simple periodic color pattern from horizontal or diagonal stripe clues, extend it across the grid with the correct phase and orientation, and validate the inferred cycle against every marker before submitting.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"task_0c1f1b2f_periodic_stripe_extrapolation","title":"Continual-ARC task-0c1f1b2f: extrapolate periodic stripe patterns","content":"For Continual-ARC task-0c1f1b2f, stripe clues encode a periodic color pattern to expand across the whole grid. Full horizontal stripes specify colors at row coordinates; infer a simple row-wise cycle and preserve its phase from the input coordinates. Diagonal stripe markers specify colors by diagonal coordinate: use r-c for down-right diagonals and r+c for the opposite slope, then extend the inferred cycle across the grid. Do not leave unmarked cells blank. Infer the period from all marker positions and colors, not from palette or spacing alone; repeated colors may occupy multiple phases. Validate that the proposed cycle reproduces every marked stripe before submitting. Verified test: parallel r-c diagonals at 5 and 10 had colors 5 and 6, respectively; the consistent period-2 field was color 6 on even r-c and color 5 on odd r-c, and submission was correct. Demonstrations included horizontal periodic sequences and diagonal periodic patterns with other periods, so do not assume period 2 universally.","path":"continual_arc","metadata":{"scope":"global","source":"five demonstrations and a correct test submission"},"reason":"Persist the demonstrated reusable procedure for inferring and extending periodic stripe patterns, including coordinate orientation, phase, and validation cautions.","after":{"id":"task_0c1f1b2f_periodic_stripe_extrapolation","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-0c1f1b2f: extrapolate periodic stripe patterns","content":"For Continual-ARC task-0c1f1b2f, stripe clues encode a periodic color pattern to expand across the whole grid. Full horizontal stripes specify colors at row coordinates; infer a simple row-wise cycle and preserve its phase from the input coordinates. Diagonal stripe markers specify colors by diagonal coordinate: use r-c for down-right diagonals and r+c for the opposite slope, then extend the inferred cycle across the grid. Do not leave unmarked cells blank. Infer the period from all marker positions and colors, not from palette or spacing alone; repeated colors may occupy multiple phases. Validate that the proposed cycle reproduces every marked stripe before submitting. Verified test: parallel r-c diagonals at 5 and 10 had colors 5 and 6, respectively; the consistent period-2 field was color 6 on even r-c and color 5 on odd r-c, and submission was correct. Demonstrations included horizontal periodic sequences and diagonal periodic patterns with other periods, so do not assume period 2 universally.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","source":"five demonstrations and a correct test submission"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:26:54.522Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:26:54.523Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929125613491","summary":"Created a global memory for the solved Continual-ARC task-3a935ce0 diagonal-periodic wallpaper rule.","rationale":"The 27×27 instance was solved correctly on the first submission, and its sparse diagonal clues consistently identified all three residue classes modulo 3.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of this task can infer the period and color assigned to each diagonal residue, tile the full grid, and validate that every clue is reproduced.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"task_3a935ce0_diagonal_periodic_wallpaper","title":"Continual-ARC task-3a935ce0: infer and tile diagonal-periodic wallpaper","content":"For Continual-ARC task-3a935ce0, sparse clues on diagonals encode a periodic wallpaper. Use diagonal coordinate d = column - row; markers on the same diagonal have the same d. Infer the period and the color assigned to each residue from the clue offsets, then fill every cell across the whole grid according to d modulo that period; do not preserve the otherwise blank background. Validated 27×27 case: color 5 appeared at d=6 (residue 0 mod 3), and color 1 appeared at d=16 (residue 1) and d=-7 (residue 2). Thus output 5 when (c-r) mod 3 == 0 and 1 otherwise. Before submitting, verify dimensions and that every visible clue agrees with its residue's assigned color. Treat period 3 and these colors as specific to the validated case; infer them from clues in future inputs.","metadata":{"scope":"global","domain":"Continual-ARC"},"reason":"The demonstrated rule was validated by a correct first-attempt solution, and recording both the reusable diagonal-residue method and the case-specific assignments supports future recurrences without overgeneralizing the palette or period.","after":{"id":"task_3a935ce0_diagonal_periodic_wallpaper","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-3a935ce0: infer and tile diagonal-periodic wallpaper","content":"For Continual-ARC task-3a935ce0, sparse clues on diagonals enco