tending it through row 12 produced the accepted answer. When a patch seems to end at a row/column with a single corrupted border cell, inspect adjacent rows and columns for a continued solid run before closing its bounds. Fill all interior outliers with the patch color and reset truly exterior specks to the current background. This accepted grid's interior corruptions included (1,2),(1,4),(4,4),(5,0),(2,11),(5,14),(6,16),(8,10),(9,7),(10,16),(9,2),(11,19); exterior noise was reset to 8. Do not assume the first visually obvious endpoint is the rectangle boundary.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:08:16.808Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:19:22.093661+00:00","version":6},"after":{"id":"task_cf510dbb_noisy_rectangular_patch_reconstruction","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-cf510dbb: restore noisy rectangular patches; validate bounds conservatively","content":"For Continual-ARC task-cf510dbb, restore intended solid, axis-aligned monochrome rectangular patches and reset isolated or non-rectangular clutter to the instance's background color. Eight demo pairs support restoring patch cells corrupted to arbitrary colors or to the background, including background-valued holes when they lie inside a rectangle supported by its other cells. Noise colors can also occur in genuine patches, so color alone does not identify clutter. Infer each rectangle's bounds from the full spatial pattern; do not extend a rectangle merely because a single adjacent noise pixel could fit an expanded box. Enumerate observed cells and candidate bounds carefully, then check every row and column of each proposed box, its interior, and cells outside all boxes. Preserve separate patches even when they share a color. The 27×24 test instance in the refinement trajectory remained unsolved after eight submissions; its guessed coordinates and edge extensions are not validated and must not be treated as a solution. When evidence leaves bounds ambiguous, retain that uncertainty rather than asserting unsupported edges.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:08:16.808Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:30:29.288Z","version":7},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682278/attempts/5f4424a6c825493ca5d3c2f501e9e3db/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
